  "caption": "Quinn's leg felt zappy, burning and tingly, and it got louder at night. Quinn's plan was to stretch it really hard. It did not enjoy that.\n\nNerve pain often feels different to muscle or joint pain: burning, electric or pins and needles, sometimes at rest or at night. Finding the cause with a proper assessment is the first step.\n\nWhat often helps: change positions and avoid long cramped postures, try gentle nerve glides little and often instead of hard stretching, keep moving and building strength, and set up a comfier sleeping position.\n\nGet checked promptly for spreading numbness, weakness, clumsiness, saddle numbness, bladder or bowel changes, or symptoms after an injury.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
